WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.157
Calculation order matters.

00:00:02.157 --> 00:00:11.547
Python follows the normal rules of arithmetic, so multiplication happens before addition unless parentheses change the

00:00:11.547 --> 00:00:18.207
grouping. Ten plus five times two becomes twenty because five times two happens first.

00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:24.652
But when we write parentheses around ten plus five, Python calculates fifteen first,

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:27.590
then multiplies by two to get thirty.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.162
Both expressions are valid. Neither produces an error.

00:00:32.162 --> 00:00:36.662
The danger is that a wrong formula can still run successfully.

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:43.336
Use parentheses when they make the intended calculation clearer for you and for anyone else reading the code.
